Though as someone that wasn't following it terribly closely, is there a core line of debate you wanted to focus on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:33:17-07:00","id":997343,"title":"","content":"not really just think that the debates taken over that thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:49:10-07:00","id":997348,"title":"","content":"Here are two things that need to be pointed out, that I think the discussion in previous thread were not discussed much.<br /> <br /> A) Garou are not vampires. They are born, they die and they are reborn into a new age. While some stay as ancestor spirits in tribal homelands, the physical living garou are still born into and (most of the time) raised in the contempolar culture of that time. Adding to this, garou do not live very long, though they could. You are old for a garou if you are in your 40s.<br /> <br /> To the actual point, most garou in the modern world are homids. Most of those homids grow up in the modern culture of their country/continent before they change, unknowing of their heritage. Even if they have ancestors, their experiences are still based on how they grew up. Even if some of these homid grumble about starting the impegrium, they are very far removed from the actual garou who began it and the situation then.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, during the times of the Impegrium, garou generally lived separate from humans and their children were raised in the knowledge of their culture. There was a much wider divide between garou and humanity in those times. That is not the case in the modern world, where garou tend to still hold ties to humanity in some way.<br /> <br /> B) The setting name is world of Darkness, but despite the name, the setting didn't stop in the 80s-90s and stay there by culture. WoD is meant to be a darker reflection of our world, and that means it reflects the current way our world is. Different themes, and so, different discussions from the previous editions (aside from W20).<br /> <br /> C) Like I said in point A, the modern garou are very far removed from their ancestors. The tribe that is the least removed, the Red Talons, is basically dying out. One could see their call for Impegrium as a way to go out in a blaze of glory rather than have their kin die out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:05:08-07:00","id":997356,"title":"","content":"It isn't so much a debate as it is Crimson and Uniform stuck on proving that all/most Garou are genocidal assholes despite all evidence to the contrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:20:19-07:00","id":997367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997356#post997356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't so much a debate as it is Crimson and Uniform stuck on proving that all/most Garou are genocidal assholes despite all evidence to the contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even on that point, even if the Garou were trying to exterminate Humanity, it wouldn't be them bringing back the Impergium. And I mentioned it in that thread, but I feel like the definition of what the Impergium was is being lost in the conversation.<br /> Even if the Garou (of any particular tribe) tried to exterminate the humans, it still wouldn't be &quot;bringing back the Impergium&quot; to me. Examples that were cited: A Wendigo Elder saying he wants to kill all Wyrmcomers (&quot;the White man&quot;) and the Get saying that they will destroy Humanity come the Apocalypse. Neither of those are &quot;bring back the Impergium&quot;. And the argument, that these examples are just the Impergium under a different name misses the point (imo) on what the Impergium actually was.<br /> <br /> You would need significant follow up (taking up systematically culling human numbers again) after whichever event decimated Humanity for it to be the Garou &quot;bringing back the Impergium&quot;. The Talons are the only ones who really argue that this is a good (or even feasible) idea.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another example brought up was a Shadowlord named &quot;Malcom the liar&quot; talking to Red Talons saying he totally agrees with them that the Impergium needs to be brought back.<br /> A) His name.<br /> B) He is a Shadowlord, agreeing with the person he's talking to.<br /> This shouldn't be used as an example of the Shadowlord tribe supporting a revival of the Impergium. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 11-02-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:44:07-07:00","id":997381,"title":"","content":"The only thing that could destroy humanity is humanity. With contemporary nuclear weapons, eighty percent of humanity could be annihilated and, more importantly for our discussion, the technological infrastructure of human civilization would be wrecked. With contemporary biological weapons, another ninety percent of humanity could be annihilated because the health infrastructure would have been annihilated. Of course, the Garou could recreate the Imperium to manage the remainder of humanity, but they would have to compete with all of the surviving supernatural creatures that need human beings to survive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:48:01-07:00","id":997384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997381#post997381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that could destroy humanity is humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, other than the advent of the Wyrm and the world ending amid brimstone and balefire as the three heads unite to destroy the Tellurian, right? Or does that count as something humans brought on themselves (not being snippy here, it could be argued that way)?<br /> <br /> Rorg's talons also could do the job nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:00:26-07:00","id":997391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997381#post997381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that could destroy humanity is humanity. With contemporary nuclear weapons, eighty percent of humanity could be annihilated and, more importantly for our discussion, the technological infrastructure of human civilization would be wrecked. With contemporary biological weapons, another ninety percent of humanity could be annihilated because the health infrastructure would have been annihilated. Of course, the Garou could recreate the Imperium to manage the remainder of humanity, but they would have to compete with all of the surviving supernatural creatures that need human beings to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Humanity being the &quot;only&quot; thing that could. There are 2 possible other examples that come to mind from the Apocalypse book. (and yes, they are purely ideas and not necessarily canon). There was a scenario where the Talons awaken a huge Earth Spirit to cause massive earthquakes to kill most of humanity. There was also Rorg tossing meteors at Earth which could work just as well. Either of those 2 (which are both associated with Red Talons) would accomplish about the same amount of destruction with similar aftereffects.<br /> <br /> For a discussion like this, it's easier to ignore other Supernaturals and not get into crossover debates (it's what all of the End books did anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:17:39-07:00","id":997555,"title":"","content":"I'm posting this here rather than the Kinfolk thread. First the Impergium is a perfect and logical result of Homo Sapiens moving out of Africa and pushing aside the Kin of the Garou and most other Fera the Neanderthal. This is indirectly referenced all through the early chapters of Shattered Dreams. As the Neanderthal faltered as a species is when the Garou turned to Homo Sapiens now how long of a span of time was this? The Ananasi sealed the deal by massacring the Neanderthal under orders from their Queen and possibly the Wyrm (If the Wyrm was still acting as the destroyer aspect this makes perfect sense as the Wyrm took things that were over) Now let's look at the tribe the one that claims credit for ending the Impergium. The CoG homeland (Mesopotamia first area impacted by the interbreeding of Neanderthal and Homo Sapiens heavily influenced by the Apis who pushed for breeding with Homo Sapiens) the CoG love to yell we wanted to end this blah, blah, blah. Now if they never persecuted the migrating Homo Sapiens perhaps this could be the real reason the Veil is lower for the CoG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:01:22-07:00","id":997566,"title":"","content":"And another thought on the Red Talons way back in the early editions there was a line about the Red Talons Homid form resembling Neanderthals. Now Griffon is also the totem of extinct creatures, perhaps taking on this aspect as the Red Talons refused to give up their kin the Neanderthal and breed with the new comers turning solely to wolves. Thus the hatred of Humans is born and long ago forgotten...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:39:24-07:00","id":997829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997566#post997566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thought on the Red Talons way back in the early editions there was a line about the Red Talons Homid form resembling Neanderthals. Now Griffon is also the totem of extinct creatures, perhaps taking on this aspect as the Red Talons refused to give up their kin the Neanderthal and breed with the new comers turning solely to wolves. Thus the hatred of Humans is born and long ago forgotten...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that got in for the same reason that there are so many instances of Hispo being said to be a dire wolf, i.e. very bad research. As the game moves on, the influence of old, bad research should be replaced and thus disappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:41:26-07:00","id":997865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997829#post997829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm pretty sure that got in for the same reason that there are so many instances of Hispo being said to be a dire wolf, i.e. very bad research.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always chalked the dire wolf thing up to D&amp;D. Doesn't make it any better either way though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:50:02-07:00","id":997870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997865#post997865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always chalked the dire wolf thing up to D&amp;D. Doesn't make it any better either way though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Along with Tou Mu and that one demon archer in KotE, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:25:07-07:00","id":998047,"title":"","content":"I wish I'd had space for my notes on the development of the tribes and the impergium within Shattered Dreams. Alas,they were off-topic in a crammed chapter as it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:50:02-07:00","id":998062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=998047#post998047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I'd had space for my notes on the development of the tribes and the impergium within Shattered Dreams. Alas,they were off-topic in a crammed chapter as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is unfortunate to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:52:04-07:00","id":998063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=997829#post997829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that got in for the same reason that there are so many instances of Hispo being said to be a dire wolf, i.e. very bad research. As the game moves on, the influence of old, bad research should be replaced and thus disappear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't disagree with the statement being the result of bad research. It was just a thought, and given the newest research of Humans and Neanderthal sharing genes it raised in my mind the possibility of the final insult to Griffon the birth of a Red Talon homid. Sure a Red Talon slipping and mating with a Human is a more likely explanation, but this is the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:14:56-07:00","id":998093,"title":"","content":"Yes, modern humans seem to be decended from the interbreeding of four subspecies of Homo sapiens (Archaic, Denisovan, Neanderthal, and Sapiens). The exact ratio depends on your ethnicity. Europeans, North Africans, and Southwest Asians tend to have the highest proportion of Neaderthal. Oceanians, South Asians, and Southeast Asians tend to have the highest proportion of Denisovan. East Asians and Native Americans tend to have the highest proportion of Archaic. The only pure populations of Sapiens seems to be in Sub-Saharan Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:18:55-07:00","id":998232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=998093#post998093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, modern humans seem to be decended from the interbreeding of four subspecies of Homo sapiens (Archaic, Denisovan, Neanderthal, and Sapiens). The exact ratio depends on your ethnicity. Europeans, North Africans, and Southwest Asians tend to have the highest proportion of Neaderthal. Oceanians, South Asians, and Southeast Asians tend to have the highest proportion of Denisovan. East Asians and Native Americans tend to have the highest proportion of Archaic. The only pure populations of Sapiens seems to be in Sub-Saharan Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archaic are still sapiens; you'd want to call it Modern instead. Never capitalize sapiens, as it is a trivial name, even when used twice, as in Modern humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:38:09-07:00","id":998273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=998232#post998232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Archaic are still sapiens; you'd want to call it Modern instead. Never capitalize sapiens, as it is a trivial name, even when used twice, as in Modern humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia's cream on a cracker. It's a forum, man, not an undergrad thesis paper. Loosen up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:24:44-07:00","id":998331,"title":"","content":"Archaic is not the designation for anatomically modern humans (it is used in the context of this thread to identify the unclassified archaic homo sapiens subspecies that we know interbred with modern homo sapiens from genetic analysis but have yet to properly identify because we have not found the bones). Modern human beings are mostly Homo sapiens sapiens, the only existence contemporary subspecies of Homo sapiens, though there are several other subspecies who contributed to modern human beings. By the way, while capitalizing the species and subspecies names are not technically correct, it prevents confusion when you are talking to people who do not have degrees in anthropology, biology, or medicine (which I think qualifies most of the people of this forums), so it is done out of courtesy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:31:45-07:00","id":998382,"title":"","content":"From the perspective of WtA and how it stands on the cusp of the Apocalypse, and how badly humanity annihilated so many different species and desecrated the spirit realms, it seems pretty clear that stopping the Impergium was a mistake - probably the second biggest mistake the Werewolves ever committed next to the War of Rage. On the other hand, the cat's kind of out of the bag at this point and you can't really restart the Impergium on a grand scale so werewolves today just have to go with the hand they were dealt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:53:54-07:00","id":998580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=998232#post998232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Archaic are still sapiens; you'd want to call it Modern instead. Never capitalize sapiens, as it is a trivial name, even when used twice, as in Modern humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was I on? Sapiens in that should have been called modern. Red Warrior needs sleep badly, it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:13:03-08:00","id":999725,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't like the way revised and W20 depict what the Garou believe of the Impergium.<br /> Garou should be proud members of a proud lineage of ancestors, who more often than not, are bigger than life paragons of virtue. It is not as if the Garou had adopted Renown recently. Wisdom and Honour probably were already around back in prehistoric times. So, I used to interpret the Garou's culling of humans as exactly that. An occasionally occurring event, when Garou travelled to the nearest settlement and killed those who weren't protected. Sure, their decisions might not have been that informed, but they weren't random either. It was about their belief, that the land could not sustain that amount of humans, so the Garou culled as humans cull herds of sheep and other animals. Obviously, the practice was not perfect, but source material tells us, that the motion to end the Impergium was discussed at great lenght. It's in not said, that the Silverfang, in his hybris, agreed to a contest of gamecraft and was bested by the Stargazer, who appeard as the enigmatic trump card. It is, imo, implied that both factions came to a standstil because the pros and cons of both sides were compelling arguments. And the leaders who had gathered there were smart and clever leaders and the spokespeople of their respective tribes.<br /> <br /> What, imo, makes no sense is killing humans for fun, keeping them as cattle or slaves, terrorizing them for fun. Sure, humans can be bullies and that is a natural phenomenon, but the majority of Garou back then was lupus born and such behaviour is not normally found in the animal kingdom. Therefore I think it doesn't really fit the Garou mindset as presented.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:06:59-08:00","id":999851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999725#post999725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't like the way revised and W20 depict what the Garou believe of the Impergium.<br /> Garou should be proud members of a proud lineage of ancestors, who more often than not, are bigger than life paragons of virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Why</i>?<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's literally <i>no</i> other supernatural in the World of Darkness that even <i>resembles</i> that ideal. That's how the <i>Garou</i> want to think of the Garou -- and it's something that makes them even <i>more</i> reprehensible. The Garou are religious fanatics that believe that they are &quot;The Chosen Of Gaia&quot; and that both justifies and excuses any act no matter how vile. They're the supernatural equivalent of the Islamic State. The twist of the World of Darkness is that the forces they're fighting against are actually <i>worse</i> -- but that in no way makes them somehow virtuous.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...Wisdom and Honour probably were already around back in prehistoric times. So, I used to interpret the Garou's culling of humans as exactly that. An occasionally occurring event, when Garou travelled to the nearest settlement and killed those who weren't protected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honor? Really?<br /> <br /> \u200bOkay, so tomorrow is Election Day over here in the States. So, let's say (complete hypothetical, mind) I go out with a rifle and assassinate Donald Trump at his next rally because I think he would be a disaster for world peace.<br /> <br /> Murdering someone for my own beliefs would be <i>honorable</i>, would it?<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was about their belief, that the land could not sustain that amount of humans, so the Garou culled as humans cull herds of sheep and other animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd the fact that there are somewhere north of five billion humans on this, the planet of Earth and somehow the world still hasn't ended -- what does that say about the Garou going the random-slaughter route thousands of years ago with human populations a fraction of today's?<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, imo, makes no sense is killing humans for fun, keeping them as cattle or slaves, terrorizing them for fun. Sure, humans can be bullies and that is a natural phenomenon, but the majority of Garou back then was lupus born and such behaviour is not normally found in the animal kingdom. Therefore I think it doesn't really fit the Garou mindset as presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously dude, have you ever seen how wolves behave when feeding from a kill or when a female comes into heat? Violence and bloodshed is part of their daily life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:38:38-08:00","id":999923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bThere's literally <i>no</i> other supernatural in the World of Darkness that even <i>resembles</i> that ideal. That's how the <i>Garou</i> want to think of the Garou -- and it's something that makes them even <i>more</i> reprehensible. The Garou are religious fanatics that believe that they are &quot;The Chosen Of Gaia&quot; and that both justifies and excuses any act no matter how vile. They're the supernatural equivalent of the Islamic State. The twist of the World of Darkness is that the forces they're fighting against are actually <i>worse</i> -- but that in no way makes them somehow virtuous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just an observation, but you don't seem to like the game much and you have an incredibly grim view of the protagonists.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bHonor? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of their Renown categories.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bAnd the fact that there are somewhere north of five billion humans on this, the planet of Earth and somehow the world still hasn't ended -- what does that say about the Garou going the random-slaughter route thousands of years ago with human populations a fraction of today's?</div> </div> </div> </div>In game, the world is pretty close to ending and generally kind of in a crap state. That's kind of the point. It might have been a mistake ending the Impergium (as an OOC point of view). I'm not sure what your argument is on this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:41:05-08:00","id":999955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999923#post999923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an observation, but you don't seem to like the game much...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b?<br /> ?!<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...and you have an incredibly grim view of the protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUm... only if your character is one of the f****d-up religious whackos. The PCs (and some occasional NPCs) are supposed to be the good guys -- not the Garou at large. For instance, in Silver Fangs, King Albrecht goes off on Whiteheart because he's basically justifying both the Impergium and War of Rage (specifically that they were mistakes only in their unintended consequences -- not because they were in any way immoral). In that bit Albrecht basically acknowledges that that's the Tribal viewpoint -- and an endless source of frustration for him. He's a signature character, but specifically because he's not representative of the tribe. The Renewalist camp loves him because he bucks the trend and calls the rest of the Tribe out on their bullshit. That's sort of where the PCs are (or ought to be). Constantly having to question their own actions when the rest of their tribes are not fabulously better than their adversaries.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of their Renown categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, and &quot;honor&quot; in the parlance of the Garou is an utterly alien concept in human terms. How does slaughtering innocent people even remotely rate as honorable?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game, the world is pretty close to ending and generally kind of in a crap state. That's kind of the point. It might have been a mistake ending the Impergium (as an OOC point of view). I'm not sure what your argument is on this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if the world still hasn't ended with over five billion humans on it -- how do the Garou justify slaughtering people with a total global population of (maybe) a million at the time? Put it another way: Culling humans was fine -- but the Kin were exempted from the culling. What was it that the average human was doing (thousands of years ago) that the average Kin was not? In the case of the former, having children was decidedly not okay. In the case of the latter, they're subject to social shaming (if not physical abuse) if they don't produce as many children as biologically possible. That's my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:13:33-08:00","id":999968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because if the world still hasn't ended with over five billion humans on it -- how do the Garou justify slaughtering people with a total global population of (maybe) a million at the time? Put it another way: Culling humans was fine -- but the Kin were exempted from the culling. What was it that the average human was doing (thousands of years ago) that the average Kin was not? In the case of the former, having children was decidedly not okay. In the case of the latter, they're subject to social shaming (if not physical abuse) if they don't produce as many children as biologically possible. That's my point. </div> </div> </div>I think the line of thinking is that, had the Impergium not been ended previously, the world wouldn't be in the current situation. Which is to say, near ending. Had humans never been allowed the foothold they currently have then Gaia might not be so close to destruction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:28:33-08:00","id":999980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYeah, and &quot;honor&quot; in the parlance of the Garou is an utterly alien concept in human terms. How does slaughtering innocent people even remotely rate as honorable?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're unknowingly threatening a precious, nearly-lost sacred place (that tenet of the litany is ironclad), but on few, read pretty much no other, occasions. Protecting a helpless human from a threat (presumably not from wild animals trying to eat them, but from clear monsters, materialized banes, and the like) gets you a bit of Honor, whereas just letting them die will cost you about as much. It's right there on the Renown chart.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because if the world still hasn't ended with over five billion humans on it -- how do the Garou justify slaughtering people with a total global population of (maybe) a million at the time? </div> </div> </div>Domestication of what were, at the time, the majority of their kinfolk. Crowding out other animals that the wolves preyed on in an area. Eventually, anthropogenic extinctions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Put it another way: Culling humans was fine -- but the Kin were exempted from the culling. What was it that the average human was doing (thousands of years ago) that the average Kin was not? In the case of the former, having children was decidedly not okay. In the case of the latter, they're subject to social shaming (if not physical abuse) if they don't produce as many children as biologically possible. That's my point. </div> </div> </div>There wasn't much of a way that kin wouldn't be exempt. In a situation where they could either be complete monsters to both sides of their being and slay their own family, or end up as hypocrites, they chose the latter, because they decided that sharing the blood was important. It was also likely a strong defensive impulse on the part of those who did have family among the humans. It wasn't enough to end things on its own, then; only shield a few, here and there. Some might have even used that as a loophole to have lots of human children and then declare larger numbers of humans as off-limits. That's pretty much the only way that things would have swung around to ending it, which they eventually did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:44:10-08:00","id":1000018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999980#post999980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they're unknowingly threatening a precious, nearly-lost sacred place...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd thus, making my point for me.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Protecting a helpless human from a threat (presumably not from wild animals trying to eat them, but from clear monsters, materialized banes, and the like) gets you a bit of Honor, whereas just letting them die will cost you about as much...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, in other words -- doing battle with the forces of the Wyrm. So which is the &quot;Honor&quot; coming from? Doing what they're designed to do, or protecting the human? Because if they don't get the Honor award if it's wild animals... Like, you see the hypocrisy, right?<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Domestication of what were, at the time, the majority of their kinfolk. Crowding out other animals that the wolves preyed on in an area...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, emphatically <i>NOT</i> due to population issues, in other words -- Just whenever the humans' activities were inconvenient to the Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There wasn't much of a way that kin wouldn't be exempt. In a situation where they could either be complete monsters to both sides of their being and slay their own family, or end up as hypocrites, they chose the latter, because they decided that sharing the blood was important. It was also likely a strong defensive impulse on the part of those who did have family among the humans. It wasn't enough to end things on its own, then; only shield a few, here and there. Some might have even used that as a loophole to have lots of human children and then declare larger numbers of humans as off-limits. That's pretty much the only way that things would have swung around to ending it, which they eventually did.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are you <i>acknowledging</i> that the Garou's justification for the culling was complete bullshit, given their concurrent attitude towards Kinfolk procreation? Or did I misread that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:36:18-08:00","id":1000137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000018#post1000018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd thus, making my point for me.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bSo, in other words -- doing battle with the forces of the Wyrm. So which is the &quot;Honor&quot; coming from? Doing what they're designed to do, or protecting the human? Because if they don't get the Honor award if it's wild animals... Like, you see the hypocrisy, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think they get more Honor for defending wild animals. At least, for wolves, definitely. The chart's in the book; you can read it too, right?<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bSo, emphatically <i>NOT</i> due to population issues, in other words -- Just whenever the humans' activities were inconvenient to the Garou. </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to say because of how weird things can get with tales of the Impergium. Somehow, there were cities before cities were really very commonplace, so there were more humans due, likely, to supernatural influences helping them to grow in numbers that might have put significant stresses on their much more local environments. Especially if they start mining for and refining gold, since that's one activity that's toxic as hell, using mercury to refine it and all.<br /> <br /> (There's a fair amount of anachronism that seems to go around, likely, again, due to shenanigans with spirits or other monsters or something else, The Garou themselves often had prophecies of calamities driving them, too, like with the Signs of the Phoenix, and the Mokole knew the path that a civilization might go down due to having been around the block a few times).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, are you <i>acknowledging</i> that the Garou's justification for the culling was complete bullshit, given their concurrent attitude towards Kinfolk procreation? Or did I misread that? </div> </div> </div>You're lumping way too many disparate details into a single aggregate and spread over a vast stretch of time, there. It doesn't return a meaningful thesis if you're trying to make a point relying on what are essentially rebellious elements of the Garou's culture trying to change it as evidence that they're hypocrites when they're trying to change things. Perhaps I should have said earlier, but the subject is running thin and you continue to refuse any notion that the werewolves are capable of genuinely changing their minds, even over tens of thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:46:41-08:00","id":1000142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bUm... only if your character is one of the f****d-up religious whackos. The PCs (and some occasional NPCs) are supposed to be the good guys -- not the Garou at large.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't actually agree with this. Yes, the PCs should be the &quot;good guys&quot;. But that doesn't mean all of the rest of the Garou are supposed to be the &quot;bad guys&quot;. Like, the Garou Nation shouldn't be one big antagonist for the players. The players should be heroes amongst a (tragically) heroic people. Now that doesn't mean the Garou don't have their flaws. They most certainly do. But overall, the Nation (or any given Sept) should be trying to do the right thing. What exactly the right thing is will always be a matter of debate. Even more so in the WoD than in the real world.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For instance, in Silver Fangs, King Albrecht goes off on Whiteheart because he's basically justifying both the Impergium and War of Rage (specifically that they were mistakes only in their unintended consequences -- not because they were in any way immoral). In that bit Albrecht basically acknowledges that that's the Tribal viewpoint -- and an endless source of frustration for him. He's a signature character, but specifically because he's not representative of the tribe. The Renewalist camp loves him because he bucks the trend and calls the rest of the Tribe out on their bullshit. That's sort of where the PCs are (or ought to be). Constantly having to question their own actions when the rest of their tribes are not fabulously better than their adversaries.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is an honest question: do you think all or even most NPC Garou are generally amoral assholes who use Gaia (or their religion in general) to justify and excuse vile actions?<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bYeah, and &quot;honor&quot; in the parlance of the Garou is an utterly alien concept in human terms. How does slaughtering innocent people even remotely rate as honorable?</div> </div> </div> </div> Killing innocents is in fact dishonorable. Protecting them is honorable. I'm not sure how this question came about? Also, I in no way think that &quot;Garou honor&quot; is alien to certain human curtural concepts of honor.<br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because if the world still hasn't ended with over five billion humans on it</div> </div> </div> </div>That population is the reason the world is ending. In setting, this isn't even debatable. <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> -- how do the Garou justify slaughtering people with a total global population of (maybe) a million at the time? Put it another way: Culling humans was fine -- but the Kin were exempted from the culling. What was it that the average human was doing (thousands of years ago) that the average Kin was not?</div> </div> </div> </div> Honoring Gaia? Feeding back into the spirit of the land? I'm guess the &quot;average human&quot; was as much as asshole then as they are today. Now <i>in theory</i> Kin were taught better than that. They honored the land and spirits as the Garou do and lived in balance with the world. So as opposed to having a negative impact, they had a neutral or positive one. Mind you, there isn't a way to know any of this until a book comes out talking about it. So for now, we get to speculate.<br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the case of the former, having children was decidedly not okay. In the case of the latter, they're subject to social shaming (if not physical abuse) if they don't produce as many children as biologically possible. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to forego arguing about Garou-Kin relationships again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:55:14-08:00","id":1000191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000137#post1000137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think they get more Honor for defending wild animals. At least, for wolves, definitely. The chart's in the book; you can read it too, right?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a pretty good point. So defending a helpless human is valued by Garou society about as much as generally &quot;being truthful&quot;. Failing to defend a helpless human is roughly equivalent to speaking at moot without permission. So if you stand idly by and watch while a fomor rapes some innocent person, murders him, then eats him -- among Garou society, that's basically like &quot;bad manners&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, failing to defend a helpless wolf is <i>worse</i> than actively damaging the Veil.<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>That's</i> the Garou Nation's relationship with &quot;Honor&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Also, given the Garou Nation's notoriety for selective enforcement of the Litany, I would argue that the whole &quot;defending / not-defending a human&quot; thing is really only in there for the Children of Gaia (and<i> maybe </i>the Stargazers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that doesn't mean the Garou don't have their flaws. They most certainly do. But overall, the Nation (or any given Sept) should be trying to do the right thing. What exactly the right thing is will always be a matter of debate. Even more so in the WoD than in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOn that, we're in agreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an honest question: do you think all or even most NPC Garou are generally amoral assholes who use Gaia (or their religion in general) to justify and excuse vile actions?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe not &quot;most&quot; -- but a <i>hell</i> of a lot. Yes.<br /> <br /> Tvarivich.<br /> Fangs-First<br /> Konietzco<br /> Pink-Tom<br /> Spotlight<br /> Bone-Juice<br /> \u200bOksanna Yahnivna<br /> Whiteheart<br /> Storm-Eye<br /> <br /> And those are just the ones that immediately spring to mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing innocents is in fact dishonorable. Protecting them is honorable. I'm not sure how this question came about? Also, I in no way think that &quot;Garou honor&quot; is alien to certain human curtural concepts of honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Impergium and whacking any humans that stray too near a caern. That's how that question came about.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, if you agree that's dishonorable, then we appear to be in agreement (but that's not the Garou as written). As written, the Garou's entire concept of &quot;Honor&quot; is seriously alien to most normal people in much the same sense that Islamic State finds kidnapping women and raping them to be &quot;honorable&quot; (because they're the Chosen Warriors of God, and -- their interpretation of -- the Koran says it's okay) is utterly alien even to the vast majority of Muslims.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Upon re-reading that last sentence, I don't like how I worded that. Let's pretend I said: &quot;Daesh is saying that's perfectly &quot;honorable&quot;, but most normal Muslims are calling bullshit&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That population is the reason the world is ending. In setting, this isn't even debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay. So it's Humanity that's going to free itself from the Weaver's Webs and consume all of creation on both sides of the Gauntlet, huh? Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-08-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:15:40-08:00","id":1000229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere's literally <i>no</i> other supernatural in the World of Darkness that even <i>resembles</i> that ideal. That's how the <i>Garou</i> want to think of the Garou -- and it's something that makes them even <i>more</i> reprehensible. The Garou are religious fanatics that believe that they are &quot;The Chosen Of Gaia&quot; and that both justifies and excuses any act no matter how vile. They're the supernatural equivalent of the Islamic State. The twist of the World of Darkness is that the forces they're fighting against are actually <i>worse</i> -- but that in no way makes them somehow virtuous.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bExcept that they are. And except that they punish those who don't respect the other parts of creation.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense, for a spiritual, sane person to acknowledge to be spiritual heir to ancestors who were vile people.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOkay, so tomorrow is Election Day over here in the States. So, let's say (complete hypothetical, mind) I go out with a rifle and assassinate Donald Trump at his next rally because I think he would be a disaster for world peace.<br /> <br /> Murdering someone for my own beliefs would be <i>honorable</i>, would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, one US state on that day votes to repeal its ban on the death sentence. So, it is not honourable if you decide to kill Trump, but if 12 jurors come to the same conclusion, it might be lawful. And carrying out the order of a court might be honourable. In the end, someone is still dead.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd the fact that there are somewhere north of five billion humans on this, the planet of Earth and somehow the world still hasn't ended -- what does that say about the Garou going the random-slaughter route thousands of years ago with human populations a fraction of today's?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, but that is hindsight.<br /> Also, arguably, the world is still dying.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999851#post999851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously dude, have you ever seen how wolves behave when feeding from a kill or when a female comes into heat? Violence and bloodshed is part of their daily life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you?<br /> There are rarely wolves killed, when establishing mating pairings and usually wolves don't kill other animals and not eat them to some degree (that is unless other animals make them leave their kill).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honoring Gaia? Feeding back into the spirit of the land? I'm guess the &quot;average human&quot; was as much as asshole then as they are today. Now <i>in theory</i> Kin were taught better than that. They honored the land and spirits as the Garou do and lived in balance with the world. So as opposed to having a negative impact, they had a neutral or positive one. Mind you, there isn't a way to know any of this until a book comes out talking about it. So for now, we get to speculate. </div> </div> </div>Actually, there is an example in the Setting. The Pure Lands and the American tribes before the white settlers came. With banes, nunnehi and other supernaturals it wasn't necessarily a safe or wyrm-free land, but it was way more balanced and healthy.<br /> That said, most native american people within the Setting were more spiritual and in-tune with nature - in a way suitable for kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:37:33-08:00","id":1000232,"title":"","content":"would have liked some info on the development of the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:05:55-08:00","id":1000290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=999955#post999955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bUm... only if your character is one of the f****d-up religious whackos. The PCs (and some occasional NPCs) are supposed to be the good guys -- not the Garou at large. For instance, in Silver Fangs, King Albrecht goes off on Whiteheart because he's basically justifying both the Impergium and War of Rage (specifically that they were mistakes only in their unintended consequences -- not because they were in any way immoral).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in game, Gaia never intended there werewolves (or any of the Fera) to be &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; Werewolves were created with specific duties that were deemed necessary for the good of Gaia (I mean, let's not forget that Gaia created an entire race, the Ratkin, specifically to spread disease and plague among humans). Early werewolves took &quot;honor&quot; from performing their duties well and fulfilling the role given to them by Gaia. This meant things like culling humans, helping to keep their population at a reasonable number and ensuring that they didn't begin using &quot;weaver tricks&quot; in ways that would harm Gaia. <br /> <br /> Ideas like 'good', 'evil', 'moral' or 'immoral' actions played no part in the way in which Gaia originally envisioned the Garou. Of course, as the Wyrm fell into corruption and its role in the world changed from Destroyer to Corrupter, the werewolves found themselves forced into the role of challenging the Wyrm. And as the werewolves changed in response to their enemy, human ideas of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; began to become more prominent. But these ideas, that some actions were morally wrong even if that's what Gaia wanted, ended up leading to the end of the Impergium, later to the War of Rage and now the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:53:31-08:00","id":1000306,"title":"","content":"Uniform, all your posts make me think you doesn't grasp the Garou mindset, past or present. It is like you are incapable of seeing matters like the Impergium from any moral vantage point other than the 21st century 'human' one, IE, your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:10:31-08:00","id":1000399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000290#post1000290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, in game, Gaia never intended there werewolves (or any of the Fera) to be &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; Werewolves were created with specific duties that were deemed necessary for the good of Gaia (I mean, let's not forget that Gaia created an entire race, the Ratkin, specifically to spread disease and plague among humans). Early werewolves took &quot;honor&quot; from performing their duties well and fulfilling the role given to them by Gaia. This meant things like culling humans, helping to keep their population at a reasonable number and ensuring that they didn't begin using &quot;weaver tricks&quot; in ways that would harm Gaia.<br /> <br /> Ideas like 'good', 'evil', 'moral' or 'immoral' actions played no part in the way in which Gaia originally envisioned the Garou. Of course, as the Wyrm fell into corruption and its role in the world changed from Destroyer to Corrupter, the werewolves found themselves forced into the role of challenging the Wyrm. And as the werewolves changed in response to their enemy, human ideas of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; began to become more prominent. But these ideas, that some actions were morally wrong even if that's what Gaia wanted, ended up leading to the end of the Impergium, later to the War of Rage and now the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:58:37-08:00","id":1000421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000191#post1000191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b The Impergium and whacking any humans that stray too near a caern. That's how that question came about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing humans that stray to close to a Caern (presumably accidentally) isn't my default assumption. It's obviously an option, but turning them away through mundane, and then supernatural means seems the more obvious first choice. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000191#post1000191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b Now, if you agree that's dishonorable, then we appear to be in agreement (but that's not the Garou as written). As written, the Garou's entire concept of &quot;Honor&quot; is seriously alien to most normal people in much the same sense that Islamic State finds kidnapping women and raping them to be &quot;honorable&quot; (because they're the Chosen Warriors of God, and -- their interpretation of -- the Koran says it's okay) is utterly alien even to the vast majority of Muslims.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Upon re-reading that last sentence, I don't like how I worded that. Let's pretend I said: &quot;Daesh is saying that's perfectly &quot;honorable&quot;, but most normal Muslims are calling bullshit&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I mostly not going to touch this at all. But, there can be actions that are neither honorable or dishonorable. Or that are honorable for one reason while being dishonorable for another. If you fail to protect a human while ensuring the safety of a Caern you are going to have a net positive most likely. Either way, there is more nuance to the Renown system than. Not everything is black and white, as much as it would make things easier if it were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000191#post1000191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b Oh, okay. So it's Humanity that's going to free itself from the Weaver's Webs and consume all of creation on both sides of the Gauntlet, huh? Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humanity is quite possibly going to feed to Wyrm of Corruption enough that it can do worse than that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:36:30-08:00","id":1000438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000229#post1000229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bExcept that they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuh-uh!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And except that they punish those who don't respect the other parts of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich is &quot;honorable&quot; how, considering that they <i>do not allow </i>humans to know about the spiritual harm they do? Seriously, humans who breach the Veil are killed as a threat -- routinely. But they're entitled to &quot;punish&quot; people for transgressions against the spirit world (that they don't even know exists)?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't make sense, for a spiritual, sane person to acknowledge to be spiritual heir to ancestors who were vile people.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, basically your argument is (correct me if I'm wrong here) that the Silver Fangs' response to criticism of their instigation of the War of Rage (ie: Plugging their ears and screaming at the top of their lungs &quot;IT WAS FOR THE GREATER GOOD!!! THE GURAHL HAVE FALLEN TO THE WYRM!!! AND THEY WOULDN'T TEACH US GIFTS!!! THEY DESERVED TO DIE!!! PRAISE BE TO GAIA!!!&quot;) -- that that bullshit is fully appropriate because they're a &quot;spiritual&quot; people and actually acknowledging vile ancestors (and their actions) somehow violates the natural order?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200bYeah, but that is hindsight...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUm, yeah... no. No it isn't. You've got that <i>exactly</i> 180 degrees backwards. Using something that happened thousands of years later as a justification for doing something when there was no immediate rationale (other than the Garou and their spirit allies <i>felt like it </i>at the time) -- <i>that's</i> hindsight.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are rarely wolves killed, when establishing mating pairings and usually wolves don't kill other animals and not eat them to some degree (that is unless other animals make them leave their kill).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn what alternate world? Wolves kill each other all the time over dominance aggression issues -- and that's not even touching on territorial disputes between packs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uniform, all your posts make me think you doesn't grasp the Garou mindset, past or present. It is like you are incapable of seeing matters like the Impergium from any moral vantage point other than the 21st century 'human' one, IE, your own. \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, so slaughtering defenseless peasants is a perfectly moral act. My problem is that I'm just failing to move the goalposts of &quot;morality&quot; far enough to acknowledge that?<br /> <br /> Wow.<br /> <br /> F***ing wow.<br /> <br /> \u200bBy that logic then, my earlier example of Daesh kidnapping and raping women is perfectly valid. Kidnapping women and raping them -- and killing them if they try to leave you is honorable, moral and just... So long as your moral vantage point says it is. Daesh are the good guys.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause (whether you realize it or not) that's the argument you just made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity is quite possibly going to feed to Wyrm of Corruption enough that it can do worse than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd whose fault is it that the shapeshifters who were supposed to keep the humans &quot;spiritual&quot; (Guhral, Apis, Grondr) all got exterminated? Whose fault is it that the humans got brutalized for three thousand years to the point that it pretty much poisoned the well with regard to Gaian spiritualism?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Garou can't set the fire and then accuse the humans of arson.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:18:44-08:00","id":1000456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuh-uh!</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think I'm done with this part of the discussion. Thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:27:26-08:00","id":1000503,"title":"","content":"Reminder: Garou only appear religious to people ignorant of all of the spirits - particularly the bad ones - that live on the other side of the world. In day to day practical existence, they are not generally religious, and in fact, a lot of them are going to be pretty far from it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:42:10-08:00","id":1000513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000232#post1000232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would have liked some info on the development of the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. I tried, but yeah, no place for it in the final book.<br /> <br /> FWIW (not much, I admit) I would have the Litany not exist in it's modern form until well after the Impergium. Through the Impergium the Changing Breeds would have other things to guide their behaviour, and prior to the Impergiums yet other things.<br /> <br /> In other words, change happens, and is natural. When the litany as it is known today is created, it served a new purpose. That it has not changed in so many years could even be a sign of Weaver Stasis - unhealthy lock in of antiquated ideas long past their relevance.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:45:11-08:00","id":1000720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so slaughtering defenseless peasants is a perfectly moral act. My problem is that I'm just failing to move the goalposts of &quot;morality&quot; far enough to acknowledge that? </div> </div> </div>If you seek to judge Garou through human morality, then their actions will seem 'evil' in some situations. But why would you? Do you judge animals in our world as evil if they kill another wolf for control of a pack?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By that logic then, my earlier example of Daesh kidnapping and raping women is perfectly valid. Kidnapping women and raping them -- and killing them if they try to leave you is honorable, moral and just... So long as your moral vantage point says it is. Daesh are the good guys. </div> </div> </div>If Islam was the actual one true religion laid down by god, then maybe? Most Garou are actual servants of the earth fighting actual monsters. While filled with flaws, they aren't exactly making it up in that sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T08:03:53-08:00","id":1000791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is &quot;honorable&quot; how, considering that they <i>do not allow</i> humans to know about the spiritual harm they do? Seriously, humans who breach the Veil are killed as a threat -- routinely. But they're entitled to &quot;punish&quot; people for transgressions against the spirit world (that they don't even know exists)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they allow humans to know of the spiritual harm they do. Their kin (who are humans) and plenty of Ggarou or kin organisations who make efforts to educate humans. Problem is, that weaver and wyrm both work against them, with their agents.<br /> It is not that mankind was not aware of climate change, extinction of animal and plant species, the dangers of fracking and what not. It is just, that the majority chooses to be ignorant in the fangs a dulling Weaver while a minority, ridden by the Wyrms greed makes everything worse.<br /> <br /> Hiding the supernatural side of their existence doesn't mean that the Garou as a people want and encourage mankind to be unaware and ignorant to Gaias problems. Children of Gaia do even celebrate seasonal rites for the Earth Mother with humans and basically, everyone who wants to join.<br /> <br /> And, at least in my games, players have gone through great lengths to make sure a person who pierced through the Veil wasn't belived by other humans, and maybe didn't believe what he saw himself, so there was no need to kill him.<br /> In either case, if the human lives or is killed to protect the Veil, still the Garou gets punished for acting against the Litany.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically your argument is (correct me if I'm wrong here) that the Silver Fangs' response to criticism of their instigation of the War of Rage (ie: Plugging their ears and screaming at the top of their lungs &quot;IT WAS FOR THE GREATER GOOD!!! THE GURAHL HAVE FALLEN TO THE WYRM!!! AND THEY WOULDN'T TEACH US GIFTS!!! THEY DESERVED TO DIE!!! PRAISE BE TO GAIA!!!&quot;) -- that that bullshit is fully appropriate because they're a &quot;spiritual&quot; people and actually acknowledging vile ancestors (and their actions) somehow violates the natural order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the war of Rage, my beloved second historical Setting aspect. It is as great a story as nuclear weaponry in Iraq.<br /> <br /> A Snake was corrupted. A Silver Fang was murdered. A Basted was framed. And when the Bastet hid amongst Gurahl there was no talk about them having fallen. They just did refuse to resurrect the murdered Silver Fang and hand over the Bastet, who was indeed inocent. Still, just as Luna designed there were rage scores rolled and people frenzied and in the end lot of people were dead. WWI pretty much.<br /> But just to make a few things clear. Only the (supposed) extinction of the Nagah was ever described as a real military campaign. Not counting the extinction of the were-bats centuries later. All the other bloodshed was due to local misunderstandings and occurances, and usually spawned by mistrust and frenzy. No idea, if they made a point to meet on full moons, so that the frenzy was ensured, but it kind of seems that way.<br /> The CoG TB rev. actually states, that the tribe blames themselves for the War of Rages duration, for if they had all moved on from the legendary initial incident a lot of miserey might have been prevented. But the tribe of Unicorn actually invited other tribes and fera for meeting again and again and it always went south, until they stopped and the War of Rage receded until it was no more.<br /> <br /> And what about the Wyrms role in all this? I have no idea, but given the fact, that a corrupted Fera started the whole thing I imagine His minions were not lazy in those days. And with Mage's Spirit Ways and Hammer&amp;Klaive both featuring Fetishes that allow to transform into another Fera nothing within this conflict has to be as it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, yeah... no. No it isn't. You've got that <i>exactly</i> 180 degrees backwards. Using something that happened thousands of years later as a justification for doing something when there was no immediate rationale (other than the Garou and their spirit allies <i>felt like it</i> at the time) -- <i>that's</i> hindsight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believing not feeling. The Garou believed that the humans would increase to numbers that natre could not sustain and they were right. The only reason humanity still rapes the planet is the Weaver, allowing more and more humans to exist. Without modern means we would not be able to sustain 7 billion people on earth.<br /> And the Garou didn't necessarily hold the humans to a higher standard then themselves, when they killed their weak and old. It is a rule the Garou subject themselves to in 'You shall not suffer thy people to tend your sickness'. They enforced a rule that most beings in the animal kingdom adhere to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what alternate world? Wolves kill each other all the time over dominance aggression issues -- and that's not even touching on territorial disputes between packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>In pack fights over dominance are often bloody but seldom lethal. Lone Wolves are occationally killed instead of driven off, but usually when food is rare. Alpha females are know to kill cubs by other female wolves, if they didn't manage to induce a premature labor by being aggressive to the other female.<br /> Surplus Killings are present in pretty much all predators and refer to killin more prey than there is need to eat. But, most predators return to eat later and surplus killings are most common when the snow is deep and killed prey will be good for eating several days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so slaughtering defenseless peasants is a perfectly moral act. My problem is that I'm just failing to move the goalposts of &quot;morality&quot; far enough to acknowledge that?<br /> <br /> By that logic then, my earlier example of Daesh kidnapping and raping women is perfectly valid. Kidnapping women and raping them -- and killing them if they try to leave you is honorable, moral and just... So long as your moral vantage point says it is. Daesh are the good guys.<br /> <br /> Because (whether you realize it or not) that's the argument you just made.</div> </div> </div> </div>By what logic is killing of the old and weak the same as rape?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And whose fault is it that the shapeshifters who were supposed to keep the humans &quot;spiritual&quot; (Guhral, Apis, Grondr) all got exterminated? Whose fault is it that the humans got brutalized for three thousand years to the point that it pretty much poisoned the well with regard to Gaian spiritualism?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, mankind can't believe in Gaia or act with respect for nature because of the Impergium? That's a leap. I mean in the real world mankind doesn't fare that well with nature, too - and there is neither Garou nor the Wyrm to blame....<br /> <br /> And the Gondr were trying to police other Fera but didn't really question there own actions that often.<br /> The Apis were the ones who, when claims of Wyrm-taint arose, tried to prove their wothiness through duels with Garou, as if that was a good idea.<br /> The Gurahl went to sleep, instead of resurrecting the fallen. Had they resurrected the Silver Fang prince in the first place, the whole thing would not have happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000438#post1000438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou can't set the fire and then accuse the humans of arson.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't the humans take responsibility for their own actions?<br /> Like I wrote before, it worked for the most part in the Pure Lands. So it is not the inability of the humans, but the unwillingness to live with Gaia that makes them a problem for everybody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:03:00-08:00","id":1000947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000290#post1000290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, in game, Gaia never intended there werewolves (or any of the Fera) to be &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; Werewolves were created with specific duties that were deemed necessary for the good of Gaia (I mean, let's not forget that Gaia created an entire race, the Ratkin, specifically to spread disease and plague among humans). Early werewolves took &quot;honor&quot; from performing their duties well and fulfilling the role given to them by Gaia. This meant things like culling humans, helping to keep their population at a reasonable number and ensuring that they didn't begin using &quot;weaver tricks&quot; in ways that would harm Gaia.<br /> <br /> Ideas like 'good', 'evil', 'moral' or 'immoral' actions played no part in the way in which Gaia originally envisioned the Garou. Of course, as the Wyrm fell into corruption and its role in the world changed from Destroyer to Corrupter, the werewolves found themselves forced into the role of challenging the Wyrm. And as the werewolves changed in response to their enemy, human ideas of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; began to become more prominent. But these ideas, that some actions were morally wrong even if that's what Gaia wanted, ended up leading to the end of the Impergium, later to the War of Rage and now the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Gaia's intentions are confusing. Ratkin only really come into their own with the rise of civilization which they predate by millenia. Kitsune exist to guide and cull societies so societies seem to be important on some level. <br /> <br /> And even if Gaia wanted the Imperigum it seems to have been a driving force of humanity even further from her than an effective culling and controlling situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:10:25-08:00","id":1000950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000947#post1000947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Gaia's intentions are confusing. Ratkin only really come into their own with the rise of civilization which they predate by millenia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real life civilizations, yes. The WoD seems to have occasional deviations from real life history on a number of occasions, such as by having pre-human reptile folk during the Mesozoic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:55:49-08:00","id":1000968,"title":"","content":"Well, we also have to remember that human beings have been around for 2 million years and, while we do not have any current evidence of Paleolithic human civilizations, the majority of Paleolithic people lived in the areas that were flooded when the seas rose 200 feet around 10,000 years ago. Occasionally, we find evidence of oddities in those regions, but underwater archeology is very expensive and rarely occurs except when there is significant amounts of money to be made (such as recovering the gold and silver from Spanish wrecks). Even so, there probably were Paleolithic civilizations where human populations could have 'benefited' from the attentions of the Ratkin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:03:31-08:00","id":1000970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000950#post1000950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Real life civilizations, yes. The WoD seems to have occasional deviations from real life history on a number of occasions, such as by having pre-human reptile folk during the Mesozoic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From W:TA's perspective there doesn't seem to have been Atlantises, a Hypborean Ages, even the prehuman civilizations if we taken Mokole sans Shattered Dreams as canon doesn't have those species get checked by Ratkin. The Ratkin only really seem to have much use or advantage when civilization rises around 10k or so bce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:27:01-08:00","id":1000981,"title":"","content":"The Ratkin had worth even before the rise of human civilization. Conclaves of fomori and corrupted human (and animal, but they don't get considered as highly or as often) tribes needed watching for and 'cleansing'. And the Bards were vital in guiding humans and Changing Breeds alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:33:34-08:00","id":1001031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000981#post1000981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ratkin had worth even before the rise of human civilization. Conclaves of fomori and corrupted human (and animal, but they don't get considered as highly or as often) tribes needed watching for and 'cleansing'. And the Bards were vital in guiding humans and Changing Breeds alike.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But their supposed purpose to cull humanity couldn't have been applicable until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:58:59-08:00","id":1001102,"title":"","content":"They still culled humans, they just culled other things as well, and hadn't the need to go fully Wyld in their work.<br /> Like, it's easy to cull a clan of a few dozen, and they didn't need to cull by simple slaughter - though they could still spread disease to weed out the weak (which was a corollary to the Ajaba) they could also cull by means of preventing undesirable matings (as a corollary to the Apis). They could lay down curses and prophecies that kept those they wanted safe, safe, and those they wanted to die, killed.<br /> <br /> It all went pear-shaped when they were prevented from doing these things and humanity began settling down with agriculture and forming cities and larger social constructs. This is when the Ratkin think ruh-roh, they'rre breeding like rabbits, this is unacceptable, what do we do?! Aha! Kill'em all and let Gaia sort 'em out.<br /> <br /> That then peeves the Apis who were getting rather pleased with their own efforts perhaps, and the Garou who didn't like their own kinfolk being killed off just cuz the Ratkin weren't more judicious in their culling. (Note, the Garou gave no fucks about the kin of other Breeds.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:27:19-08:00","id":1001119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000970#post1000970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> From W:TA's perspective there doesn't seem to have been Atlantises, a Hypborean Ages, even the prehuman civilizations if we taken Mokole sans Shattered Dreams as canon doesn't have those species get checked by Ratkin. The Ratkin only really seem to have much use or advantage when civilization rises around 10k or so bce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Atlantises or First Cities, no. Just cities and settlements that were bigger than one might think typical for the time. Also, if one takes humanity's original range to be the numbers it should have as intended, human &quot;overpopulation&quot; is set at a very low number to the Garou and Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:16:49-08:00","id":1001425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1000791#post1000791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, at least in my games, players have gone through great lengths to make sure a person who pierced through the Veil wasn't belived by other humans, and maybe didn't believe what he saw himself, so there was no need to kill him.<br /> In either case, if the human lives or is killed to protect the Veil, still the Garou gets punished for acting against the Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd for every Child of Gaia, there's a Red Talon on the opposite end of that spectrum. I know you've personally argued that the Get of Fenris are not as extreme as the Talons, so (although I completely disagree with that sentiment) let's see what the &quot;more moderate&quot; Get have to say on the subject, hmmm...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</b>: &quot;If the humans see you change, you must stalk and destroy them. You must leave no evidence. Be aware of your surroundings, and avoid changing shapes in public places. If Crinos is your only resort, make certain that any witnesses never have a chance to speak of the matter.&quot; Get of Fenris Tribebook page 34.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hienrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CoG TB rev. actually states, that the tribe blames themselves for the War of Rages duration, for if they had all moved on from the legendary initial incident a lot of miserey might have been prevented. But the tribe of Unicorn actually invited other tribes and fera for meeting again and again and it always went south, until they stopped and the War of Rage receded until it was no more.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHow you can even think this is a good example to support your position is utterly bewildering. Let's have a quick look:<br /> \u200b&quot;What do you mean, sister? The Children tried to help -- to save the Others! And we --' A log crackled and hissed. '-- Are at fault. The Others trusted us, and that was their undoing. I myself count six times when the bears or the crocodiles were lured to 'peace talks' with a Child of Gaia as mediator. Each time, another tribe would use the occasion for ambush...&quot; &quot;So the warrior tribes tricked us? Then it's not our fault...&quot; &quot;...It wasn't just that they tricked us, it's that we kept trying and trying to mend fences that were long since scattered ash.&quot; Child of Gaia Tribebook (revised) page 26.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's not the Children of Gaia blaming themselves for the War of Rage's duration -- that's them blaming themselves for <i>trusting their fellow Garou </i>when they should have known better. It's them offering a critique of refusing to actually look at the rest of the Garou Nation and accept what they really are. And more to the point, it's actually the perfect example of how depraved the rest of the Garou were at the time, and frankly undermines <i>your</i> position that the Garou should ignore the misdeeds of their ancestors as somehow not thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what logic is killing of the old and weak the same as rape?</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple things:<br /> <br /> 1. So, the kidnapping and murder part is perfectly fine -- it's the <i>rape</i> that's the red line?<br /> <br /> \u200b2. (Ignoring the rape part for a moment.) You <i>do</i> see how Daesh kidnapping women and demanding that they bear their children because (according to their interpretation of the Koran) that's their privilege as Warriors of God -- and (again, their interpretation) the women's <i>only</i> purpose, how that draws an <i>extremely</i> uncomfortable parallel with the Garou and their Kinfolk, right?<br /> <br /> \u200b3. Okay, forget the rape part. In fact, forget the women entirely. Kidnapping and murdering the men... Kidnapping and murdering innocent and defenseless civilians solely because they're Shias, Alawites, Kurds, Yazidis, etc. -- is honorable, moral, and just? Because that's their viewpoint based on their spiritual beliefs? Is that<i> really </i>your position?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, mankind can't believe in Gaia or act with respect for nature because of the Impergium? That's a leap.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;The Garou descended upon the human settlements at night, slaying humans at their whim. While this savagery served to keep the human population steady, it also ensured that the humans hated and feared the werewolves. This fear eventually drove them to find dread allies. The Wyrm readily accepted humans who sought power. The first undead and dark sorcerers rose to power, and these godlike entities could slay even Gaia's Chosen. They offered humans protection from the monsters...&quot; &quot;...The Impergium changed humans. They no longer wished to live in harmony with nature. They wanted vengeance against it...&quot; &quot;... Werewolves had driven humans to the enemies of Gaia.&quot; Dark Ages Werewolf, Page 33.<br /> <br /> No it's <i>not</i> a leap. It's the friggin' setting. As written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:10:08-08:00","id":1001453,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the Daesh are really a perversion of the Garou (at least according to the Garou Nation), as they are Garou who believe in Allah rather than in Gaia. As for the Imperium, it was a mistake for the Garou to try to regulate human populations instead of allowing the Ratkin to regulate human populations, I do not think that anyone can disagree with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:13:56-08:00","id":1001454,"title":"","content":"A quick thing or 2<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd for every Child of Gaia, there's a Red Talon on the opposite end of that spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>For every Red Talon, there are 3-4 Children of Gaia <i>at least</i>. Talons are the smallest tribe, possibly alongside the Stargazers, while Children of Gaia are one of the largest tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you've personally argued that the Get of Fenris are not as extreme as the Talons, so (although I completely disagree with that sentiment) let's see what the &quot;more moderate&quot; Get have to say on the subject, hmmm...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</b>: &quot;If the humans see you change, you must stalk and destroy them. You must leave no evidence. Be aware of your surroundings, and avoid changing shapes in public places. If Crinos is your only resort, make certain that any witnesses never have a chance to speak of the matter.&quot; Get of Fenris Tribebook page 34.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is laughable that you are using the Get as a &quot;moderate&quot; Tribe.<br /> <br /> Even with that though: &quot;Be aware of your surroundings, and avoid changing shapes in public places. If Crinos is your only resort&quot;. That section of the statement is actually kind of important. So do everything you can to not have to change, but if you do change in publin (which breaks the Litany), you need to make sure to do everything to protect your people (the point of the Veil). This doesn't in any way imply that you aren't going to lose both Wisdom and Honor Renown (at minimum). They aren't saying you get a free pass for killing whoever you want. And again, this isn't a moderate Tribe. Get tend to be on the extreme end for everything they do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:48:53-08:00","id":1001469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001454#post1001454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For every Red Talon, there are 3-4 Children of Gaia <i>at least</i>. Talons are the smallest tribe, possibly alongside the Stargazers, while Children of Gaia are one of the largest tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd how exactly does that justify using the Children as the average for the Garou, when they're clearly on opposite ends of the spectrum from the Talons? No. If heinrich wants to use the Children of Gaia as an example of how the <i>average</i> Garou behaves, then<i> I</i> get to use the Talons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is laughable that you are using the Get as a &quot;moderate&quot; Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm... mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm... Yep. Sort of the point I was making. (It's called &quot;sarcasm&quot;)<br /> <br /> So, I take it we're in agreement that that's sort of a silly idea, right?<br /> <br /> \u200bAs in, the next time heinrich says something absurd like that, you guys aren't going to reflexively give him a &quot;like&quot; and then agree with him? Just saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with that though: &quot;Be aware of your surroundings, and avoid changing shapes in public places. If Crinos is your only resort&quot;. That section of the statement is actually kind of important. So do everything you can to not have to change, but if you do change in publin (which breaks the Litany), you need to make sure to do everything to protect your people (the point of the Veil). This doesn't in any way imply that you aren't going to lose both Wisdom and Honor Renown (at minimum). They aren't saying you get a free pass for killing whoever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich would be a convincing argument if that was <i>actually</i> the point that I was responding to. Heinrich took exception to my statement that Garou routinely murder humans who breach the Veil. And for every Child of Gaia (not being sarcastic this time) there's a Red Talon, Shadow Lord, or Get of Fenris on the other side of that spectrum (actually, probably more). And they <i>do</i> routinely kill people who see stuff the Garou don't want them to see.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I got preoccupied with responding to idpersona and forgot to respond to this:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the Daesh are really a perversion of the Garou (at least according to the Garou Nation), as they are Garou who believe in Allah rather than in Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um, I think you're thinking of something else. Daesh are real-life human beings (if perhaps not <i>humane</i> beings), not World of Darkness werewolves. Unless I'm misunderstanding your quote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:35:17-08:00","id":1001523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001469#post1001469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ummm... mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm... Yep. Sort of the point I was making. (It's called &quot;sarcasm&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sarcasm is often times hard to read on the internet. Apologies for missing it on the Get example.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001469#post1001469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I take it we're in agreement that that's sort of a silly idea, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That Get are &quot;moderate&quot; Garou? Sure. Though I didn't see where that was said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001469#post1001469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bWhich would be a convincing argument if that was <i>actually</i> the point that I was responding to. Heinrich took exception to my statement that Garou routinely murder humans who breach the Veil. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that is supposed to read as &quot;Garou who breach the Veil routinely murder humans&quot;.<br /> If that's what you meant, then I would say that Garou who routinely break the Litany don't last long. I would have to go back and read all of the Tribebook views on the Veil part of the Litany for specifics, but to point out: willing to kill humans to protect the Veil is not the same as enjoying doing it (which seems to be how you present it). They kind of <i>have to</i> to protect themselves. And there are punishments in place for situations coming to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001469#post1001469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And for every Child of Gaia (not being sarcastic this time) there's a Red Talon, Shadow Lord, or Get of Fenris on the other side of that spectrum (actually, probably more). And they <i>do</i> routinely kill people who see stuff the Garou don't want them to see..</div> </div> </div> </div>Already pointed out that the Get do so as a last resort.<br /> And I actually see zero problem with the idea of killing a human here and there to protect the Veil (the Veil is vital, individuals humans generally aren't). But it's important to realize that the Garou (outside of the Talons) aren't doing so gleefully. It's duty. But the situation coming to that means someone failed somewhere and is going to lose Renown at the very least.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:58:13-08:00","id":1001532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001523#post1001523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming that is supposed to read as &quot;Garou who breach the Veil routinely murder humans&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo. Garou routinely murder humans who breach the Veil. That is humans who are witnesses to an incident involving Garou and trying to raise the alarm that werewolves are a thing (remember that one out of every two hundred humans are completely immune to the Delerium and have no Veil). Those humans are simply killed whenever they start talking about what they've seen. Also, for some of the tribes closer to the Talon end of the spectrum, this issue is seen as having a simplistic solution. If <i>any</i> human might be immune to the Delerium, the standard response (for the Get, it's actually tribal policy) is to kill <i>all</i> humans who witness Garou in Crinos form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I actually see zero problem with the idea of killing a human here and there to protect the Veil (the Veil is vital, individuals humans generally aren't). But it's important to realize that the Garou (outside of the Talons) aren't doing so gleefully. It's duty. But the situation coming to that means someone failed somewhere and is going to lose Renown at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's a more complicated issue, and I would argue with some of the assumptions there. But that's not where the discussion was going (losing Renown for breaching the Veil). The argument was being made that Garou don't murder humans who find out that Garou exist, but rather focus their efforts on discrediting them. That might be the general approach of the Children of Gaia, but it's not the<i> average </i>Garou. And I would argue that even if a pack (even quite a few Children of Gaia) were to take that approach initially, if it failed and then intimidation failed, <i>eventually</i> they're going to kill the human.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:51:45-08:00","id":1001558,"title":"","content":"I think that the Wendigo and the Uktenu do not kill Native Americans who witness things (and would probably lethally oppose any Garou that tried to do so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T18:38:49-08:00","id":1001578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001532#post1001532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNo. Garou routinely murder humans who breach the Veil. That is humans who are witnesses to an incident involving Garou and trying to raise the alarm that werewolves are a thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I've never heard the Veil term being used the way you are using it. We are meaning the same thing in any case.<br /> But the way it's said makes a difference. And admittedly, this could just be me and the groups I've played with, I fully acknowledge that. But the Veil being breached is never on the humans. Garou can breach the Veil by getting caught. Putting it that way, puts the blame (and responsibility) squarely on the Garou in question. This is a bit of a tangent though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001532#post1001532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The argument was being made that Garou don't murder humans who find out that Garou exist, but rather focus their efforts on discrediting them. That might be the general approach of the Children of Gaia, but it's not the<i> average</i> Garou. And I would argue that even if a pack (even quite a few Children of Gaia) were to take that approach initially, if it failed and then intimidation failed, <i>eventually</i> they're going to kill the human.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Having to kill</i> to protect the Veil is actually part of the punishment for breaching it. If all else fails, the Garou <i>have to</i> fix the problem, by any means necessary. They aren't doing it for fun. It is a necessity of survival. If it comes down to it. Garou are expected to be smarter than that. They are expected to protect the Veil. They are also expected to protect people actually. That is also in their Litany. But sometimes things happen and you have to make a choice. 2 of the tenets of the Litany can't afford to be broken, and the Veil is one of them. So Garou will take the Renown hit and possible punishment Rites and social stigma of having fucked up and they will kill the human whose knowledge threatens them. Again though, that isn't a decision that gets come to easily. Having to come to that point means the Garou screwed things up a few times already.<br /> <br /> Edit: I just flipped through every Revised Tribebook. The only 2 books (besides Talons) that mention killing humans because the Veil was breached are the Get and the Furies. And both of them frame it as a duty/punishment. None of the other 11 books mention it. So throwing the Shadowlords in there is misleading. I certainly wouldn't say they are above killing to protect the Veil, but they pride themselves on subtlety and misdirection. I would imagine there being harsh penalties among the Tribe for so blatantly failing to follow the Litany.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 11-10-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T21:32:06-08:00","id":1001622,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, and I think that the majority of Tribes evaluate things based on the level of threat from the human. The majority of people will be considered insane when they start talking about werewolves in modern society and will probably be committed so that they can be treated for their delusions. It is more risky to the Veil to kill them than to let them rave. It is the ones who are come back with friends that are the threat, but there are many ways to quietly kill humans without much violence. Poison is suitable, since there is no honor to be gained from their deaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:05:19-08:00","id":1001651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001622#post1001622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree, and I think that the majority of Tribes evaluate things based on the level of threat from the human. The majority of people will be considered insane when they start talking about werewolves in modern society and will probably be committed so that they can be treated for their delusions. It is more risky to the Veil to kill them than to let them rave...</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree. It's a nice sentiment, but with DNA, SAD, the Inquisition, various intelligence services like the NSA and what-have-you running around, an individual human actually becomes a threat. This is made worse by the little complication that whatever supernatural thing that was the impetus for going Crinos-Postal in the first place, is not the <i>only</i> supernatural threat in the world. So, if it was a pack of Black Spirals that made the Garou breach the Veil, if a human starts babbling about the werewolves (even if no other <i>human</i> believes him), you can bet that the vampires will. You can bet Hunters will. You can bet the Technocracy will. In many cases, it really is easier to just murder the human and be done with it -- and if it's easy and the only down side is a dead human (which from the Garou perspective, there's plenty more where they came from), which tact do you think they're going to take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:04:38-08:00","id":1001681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<b>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</b>: &quot;If the humans see you change, you must stalk and destroy them. You must leave no evidence. Be aware of your surroundings, and avoid changing shapes in public places. If Crinos is your only resort, make certain that any witnesses never have a chance to speak of the matter.&quot; Get of Fenris Tribebook page 34.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a nice quote of a extremist tribe that by no means takes into account that the Veil has a component that makes humans forget/rationalise what happened. Even the Get should know that, even if the author of the book conveniently forgot to make the tribe look more badass with that statement.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bHow you can even think this is a good example to support your position is utterly bewildering. Let's have a quick look:<br /> \u200b&quot;What do you mean, sister? The Children tried to help -- to save the Others! And we --' A log crackled and hissed. '-- Are at fault. The Others trusted us, and that was their undoing. I myself count six times when the bears or the crocodiles were lured to 'peace talks' with a Child of Gaia as mediator. Each time, another tribe would use the occasion for ambush...&quot; &quot;So the warrior tribes tricked us? Then it's not our fault...&quot; &quot;...It wasn't just that they tricked us, it's that we kept trying and trying to mend fences that were long since scattered ash.&quot; Child of Gaia Tribebook (revised) page 26.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bA couple things:<br /> <br /> 1. So, the kidnapping and murder part is perfectly fine -- it's the <i>rape</i> that's the red line?<br /> <br /> \u200b2. (Ignoring the rape part for a moment.) You <i>do</i> see how Daesh kidnapping women and demanding that they bear their children because (according to their interpretation of the Koran) that's their privilege as Warriors of God -- and (again, their interpretation) the women's <i>only</i> purpose, how that draws an <i>extremely</i> uncomfortable parallel with the Garou and their Kinfolk, right?<br /> <br /> \u200b3. Okay, forget the rape part. In fact, forget the women entirely. Kidnapping and murdering the men... Kidnapping and murdering innocent and defenseless civilians solely because they're Shias, Alawites, Kurds, Yazidis, etc. -- is honorable, moral, and just? Because that's their viewpoint based on their spiritual beliefs? Is that<i> really </i>your position?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't condone any of that, and any of those practices aren't really comparable to the Impergium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNo it's <i>not</i> a leap. It's the friggin' setting. As written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my statement, that I don't like the way the Impergium is described in revised and beyond. In 2nd Edition, with what I started to play, the Impergium was often mentioned but not really described beyond: <i>The 3,000 years immediately following the birth of agriculture, during which strict population quotas were maintained on all human villages.</i><br /> <br /> Leading to my statement, that I feel the later descriptions of the Impergium do not fit with the way the garou see their ancestors and their deeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001425#post1001425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b[..]If heinrich wants to use the Children of Gaia as an example of how the <i>average</i> Garou behaves, then<i> I</i> get to use the Talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say these players played Children of Gaia, because they didn't. At least not all of them. They all played homid, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as far as humans who have breached the Veil go: Sure vampires, technocrats and what not would believe the human, but would they want to harm the garou or investigate ?<br /> The technocrats might. In any case, vampires and technocrats can wipe the humans memories and protect their worlds by that, too.<br /> So, more often than not, it is okay for garou just to take actions, so the human won't be able to convince the greater public of werewolves...<br /> In any case, there aten't any reliable figures on how often it is supposed to occure in the setting, that a human really pierces the Veil and of that instances, how often he is cilled. Sure, every one in 200 would in theory be immune to the Delirium and its aftereffect, but somehow the majority never believed one of those in all the centuries past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-11-2016, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:48:43-08:00","id":1001725,"title":"","content":"Well, look at the Internet about Bigfoot encounters in our world. I imagine that would be an example of a human encountering a Garou in Crinos form in cWoD. And I doubt the Garou go slaughtering everyone with a Bigfoot story in cWoD, as it would kind of draw attention to their existence. There are tens of thousands of lunatics in the USA, the worst thing that you can do if you do not want to draw attention is to start killing lunatics who share the same story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:56:36-08:00","id":1001842,"title":"","content":"Generally, Talons are a bad example to use in things like this, not just due to their suicidal want to die with glory rather than to wither away. But also because they lack human kinfolk, they have no worry over hurting their own family if they kill humans. All other tribes, especially ones like Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers, have to worry about killing lost kinfolk or pre-change lost cubs. Nevermind any contacts or allies.<br /> <br /> As for killing to keep the Veil, this is why garou have Gifts upon Rites upon Fetishes designed just for hiding. Apeskin and Monkey Puzzle for metis and lupus, Blurr of the Milky Eye for Ragabash. Nevermind traditions such as the High Ban that forbids any garou from shifting out of homid. Killing humans isn't the first, third,tenth or even fifteenth option. It is 'round the bottom for most tribes.<br /> <br /> Also, Uni26, are you using revised or 2nd edition tbs? Because the texts hints of latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:05:58-08:00","id":1001928,"title":"","content":"Let's review:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uniform, all your posts make me think you doesn't grasp the Garou mindset, past or present. It is like you are incapable of seeing matters like the Impergium from any moral vantage point other than the 21st century 'human' one, IE, your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so slaughtering defenseless peasants is a perfectly moral act. My problem is that I'm just failing to move the goalposts of &quot;morality&quot; far enough to acknowledge that? (...)<br /> ...\u200bBy that logic then, my earlier example of Daesh kidnapping and raping women is perfectly valid. Kidnapping women and raping them -- and killing them if they try to leave you is honorable, moral and just... So long as your moral vantage point says it is...</div> </div> </div> </div>And then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what logic is killing of the old and weak the same as rape?</div> </div> </div> </div>And then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple things:<br /> 1. So, the kidnapping and murder part is perfectly fine -- it's the rape that's the red line?<br /> (...)<br /> \u200b3. Okay, forget the rape part. In fact, forget the women entirely. Kidnapping and murdering the men... Kidnapping and murdering innocent and defenseless civilians solely because they're Shias, Alawites, Kurds, Yazidis, etc. -- is honorable, moral, and just? Because that's their viewpoint based on their spiritual beliefs? Is that really your position?</div> </div> </div> </div>And then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't condone any of that, and any of those practices aren't really comparable to the Impergium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously dude, you're putting yourself in contention for the Donald Trump Academy Awards of Doubletalk.<br /> *sigh*<br /> So let's see if I've got this right: &quot;Killing the old and weak&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of Gaia and you're allowed to do that, is fundamentally different than &quot;kidnapping and murdering innocent civilians&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of God and inherently allowed to do that?<br /> For that matter, do you feel that &quot;killing the old and weak&quot; is honorable, moral, and just?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a nice quote of a extremist tribe that by no means takes into account that the Veil has a component that makes humans forget/rationalise what happened. Even the Get should know that, even if the author of the book conveniently forgot to make the tribe look more badass with that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conveniently ignoring that that's <i>not</i> what's going on there. The Get take the view that (as I've already mentioned before in this thread) since <i>any</i> human might be immune to the Delerium (.5%), the safest course of action is to kill <i>all</i> bystanders. And you can argue all you want about that actually not being a good idea, but as the Impergium shows (regardless of how much you personally want to believe that it doesn't) when given a choice where one of the choices is &quot;kill them&quot; the Garou tend to knee-jerk in one direction over <i>all</i> others.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence my statement, that I don't like the way the Impergium is described in revised and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Talons, Shadow Lords, Get of Fenris, Wendigo, and <i>all</i> of the other examples I quote are &quot;exceptions, not the rule&quot; (and yes, you <i>did</i> say that the last time we discussed this), but literally the <i>vast majority </i>of everything that has <i>ever</i> been written about Werewolf: the Apocalypse, plus all of W20 is <i>also</i> invalid?<br /> Y'know, I think Crimson may have hit the nail on the head.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as far as humans who have breached the Veil go: Sure vampires, technocrats and what not would believe the human, but would they want to harm the garou or investigate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, what version of Werewolf are you <i>playing</i>?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Uni26, are you using revised or 2nd edition tbs? Because the texts hints of latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>All. I never really picked up on there being much of a difference, really.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:10:13-08:00","id":1002326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001928#post1001928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's see if I've got this right: &quot;Killing the old and weak&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of Gaia and you're allowed to do that, is fundamentally different than &quot;kidnapping and murdering innocent civilians&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of God and inherently allowed to do that?<br /> For that matter, do you feel that &quot;killing the old and weak&quot; is honorable, moral, and just?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the WoD it might be. And, Garou don't hold themselves to a higher standard there, not forcing their people to tend their sickness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001928#post1001928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conveniently ignoring that that's <i>not</i> what's going on there. The Get take the view that (as I've already mentioned before in this thread) since <i>any</i> human might be immune to the Delerium (.5%), the safest course of action is to kill <i>all</i> bystanders. And you can argue all you want about that actually not being a good idea, but as the Impergium shows (regardless of how much you personally want to believe that it doesn't) when given a choice where one of the choices is &quot;kill them&quot; the Garou tend to knee-jerk in one direction over <i>all</i> others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, that if that was case, then either humanity or the Garou would be extinced and there wouldn't be a Veil anymore, for let's face it mass murders not happening that often.<br /> So, don't go base your whole argument on a piece of in-character text from an author who wanted the tribe he wrote about sound badass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001928#post1001928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Talons, Shadow Lords, Get of Fenris, Wendigo, and <i>all</i> of the other examples I quote are &quot;exceptions, not the rule&quot; (and yes, you <i>did</i> say that the last time we discussed this), but literally the <i>vast majority </i>of everything that has <i>ever</i> been written about Werewolf: the Apocalypse, plus all of W20 is <i>also</i> invalid?<br /> Y'know, I think Crimson may have hit the nail on the head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily invalid. But it is a addition to the 2nd Edition and readin how these addition make you think the garou are supposed to be just strenghten my belive that they were bad additions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1001928#post1001928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, what version of Werewolf are you <i>playing</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, seriously. The technocrats think they are reality deviants, but they have some power over spirits, a thing most technocrats don't really understand - so devert resources there or not ?<br /> Vampires are considered the enemy by most werewolves and vampires know that, would they make an effort to attack werewolves or would they hide in the shadows to save their skin, maybe push an enemy into the direction of the supposed piercing of the Veil ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:24:00-08:00","id":1002330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's see if I've got this right: &quot;Killing the old and weak&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of Gaia and you're allowed to do that, is fundamentally different than &quot;kidnapping and murdering innocent civilians&quot; because your spiritual beliefs teach that you are the chosen of God and inherently allowed to do that?<br /> For that matter, do you feel that &quot;killing the old and weak&quot; is honorable, moral, and just?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002326#post1002326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the WoD it might be. And, Garou don't hold themselves to a higher standard there, not forcing their people to tend their sickness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnnnnnnnnnd, I'm out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:05:16-08:00","id":1002391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002330#post1002330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnnnnnnnnnd, I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently Uniform26 can't even right now. That's ok, because this whole Impergium thing seems to boil down to all Garou are ISIS (perhaps Godwin's Law needs to be updated) because some of them killed people in prehistory and some of them want to do similar things now.<br /> <br /> It still seems like we are failing to parse the difference between a game setting and real-life morals.<br /> <br /> I am not for killing killing off the old and weak in real life, but it doesn't bother me to make a story where the heroes might hold to a more draconian or socially darwinistic point of view. If that is impossible, if brutal werewolves are so grotesque and vile, why bother playing the game? If the Impergium gets your dander up, there are lots of other opportunities for outrage in WoD. Aren't most of these game lines a minefield of moralistic fury?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T05:23:25-08:00","id":1002505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002330#post1002330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnnnnnnnnnd, I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to ask, what did you hope to gain from this discussion? If you wanted us to admit that garou were horrible in starting the Impegrium, then at least on my part, that I all ready thought so about it. Same with the War of Rage. Even if the situation was more complex than just garou being macho, they still messed stuff up badly enough that it easily cost them many fights to avoid the end times.<br /> <br /> However, I still cannot say that any Elder in the books calling for a new Impegrium or text saying that garou would a wiped humanity away if not for Children of Gaia, is entirely reflective of the whole of Garou Nation. Because garou -need- humanity far more than they need their wolf halves. Humanity gives them tools, it gives them control and it gives them allies. That is one reason, at least to me, that most tribes have leaned so much more on human than wolf halves. And that is why Red Talons are so aggressive about humanity, their only tool to keep their lands clean is to kill and drive humans away. Every other tribe has both homids AND kinfolk to do so.<br /> <br /> And you can see it in Wendigo as well. Due to their kinfolk being abused and ignored by the system, they are more likely to resort to aggressive means out of desperation. Uktena, who have chosen to widen their pool of kinfolk, are far less likely to do that. For Fenrir, for all their boasts and chest thumping, they put their kinfolk on a high pedestal and care and expect a lot from them.<br /> <br /> Another factor making modern Impegrium pretty hard, is that most of the tribes who handle the actual infrastructure of the Nation are very human reliant. Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia are a no-brainer why, but Black Furies' whole reason to exist is based on human culture. They might protect the wild places, but the fact they take their name and traditions from things tied to womanhood is entirely a human thing. Wolves do not have such issues. Silver Fangs, the kings and lords, are obsessed with lineages to the point they have -schools- set up just for their cubs and kin. For any of these tribes, another Impegrium would destroy their support networks very badly. And, as noted above, they -need- to networks to survive.<br /> <br /> There is also a story in Drums around the Fire, where a Silver Fang and a Black Fury got a nasty surprise when a village started following a Mage to avoid the wolves attacking them. It is noted that things like this ended the Impegrium.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T14:40:54-08:00","id":1002643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't like the way revised and W20 depict what the Garou believe of the Impergium.<br /> Garou should be proud members of a proud lineage of ancestors, who more often than not, are bigger than life paragons of virtue.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002505#post1002505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to ask, what did you hope to gain from this discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping to gain an acknowledgement that murdering innocent people because your faith says it's okay and because <i>you feel like it </i>is inherently at odds with being a &quot;paragon of virtue&quot;. But...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...do you feel that &quot;killing the old and weak&quot; is honorable, moral, and just?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the WoD it might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b...that doesn't seem to be in the cards. The consensus appears that murdering innocent people (so long as you do it in the World of Darkness where apparently &quot;morality&quot; is a concept so squishy that it has lost <i>all </i>meaning... <i>Laughing Stranger</i>) is honorable, noble, virtuous, and wonderful.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I'm out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:02:54-08:00","id":1002681,"title":"","content":"Since you're out (twice now, I'll assume no response will come). Either way...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002643#post1002643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was hoping to gain an acknowledgement that murdering innocent people because your faith says it's okay and because <i>you feel like it </i>is inherently at odds with being a &quot;paragon of virtue&quot;. But...</div> </div> </div> </div>Murdering innocents is obviously wrong. I don't think anyone argued otherwise. But it is simplistic to write it off as being due to religious zealotry. The world is literally on the verge of ending in the WtA's WoD. And &quot;because they feel like it&quot;? Zero people have argued that. That is a stance you've decided to argue against that isn't supported in the books. <br /> <br /> <br /> Splitting this one up a bit so it won't be a direct quote:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002643#post1002643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200b...that doesn't seem to be in the cards. The consensus appears that murdering innocent people is honorable, noble, virtuous, and wonderful.</div> </div> </div> </div>As stated above, no one argued this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002643#post1002643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200b(so long as you do it in the World of Darkness where apparently &quot;morality&quot; is a concept so squishy that it has lost <i>all </i>meaning... <i>Laughing Stranger</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div> That does seem to describe morality in the WoD in general (look at VtM and what you can do on Humanity while still being a &quot;good&quot; person). It's a different world than we live in you know. At least the Garou have a reason to be and are working towards that, however flawed they are. Which btw, they were literally created by an otherworldly spirit and put on this course. That, again, isn't even arguable in setting. So maybe your argument should be that Gaia isn't benevolent enough?<br /> <br /> Curious...since you seem to be measuring Garou up against a perceived higher standard of morality from the real world, how many people do you think the average real world person would kill to save their family? Their country? The world?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002643#post1002643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bAnd I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bye for now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T18:11:12-08:00","id":1002728,"title":"","content":"The majority of people would bathe in the blood of the guilty to save their loved ones and a significant portion of them would kill innocents as well. The human impulse is to kill to protect what you love, which is why we have a justice system, to protect innocents from disproportionate retaliation.<br /> <br /> Country is more nebulous, most soldiers do not fire their guns directly at the enemy because they are psychologically unable to murder for impersonal reasons (in WW 1, they had problems getting soldiers to shoot at the enemy at all). The idea with the psychological conditioning that is basic training is to overwhelm that human impulse, so soldiers will shot and kill when ordered to.<br /> <br /> I do not think that anyone is defending the murder of innocents, and I think that I would kill off a PC who went that route. If you want to play a murder machine, you can go play FATAL or some other piece of crap game like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 11-13-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:39:28-08:00","id":1002863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That does seem to describe morality in the WoD in general (look at VtM and what you can do on Humanity while still being a &quot;good&quot; person). It's a different world than we live in you know. At least the Garou have a reason to be and are working towards that, however flawed they are. Which btw, they were literally created by an otherworldly spirit and put on this course. That, again, isn't even arguable in setting. So maybe your argument should be that Gaia isn't benevolent enough? </div> </div> </div> This really does, again, seem to be a strong point for me. Spirits and the Triat do exist and have a very real impact on the world. So the idea that they are acting out of faith isn't quite accurate in comparing them to ISIS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:44:50-08:00","id":1002956,"title":"","content":"A 'good' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 8+, a 'normal' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 4-7, and a 'bad' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 3-. A 'good' person cannot accidentally break someone's arm without checking for degeneration. A 'normal' person cannot assassinate someone without checking for degeneration. A 'bad' person can do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:47:04-08:00","id":1002990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002956#post1002956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 'good' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 8+, a 'normal' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 4-7, and a 'bad' person in VtM is someone with Humanity 3-. A 'good' person cannot accidentally break someone's arm without checking for degeneration. A 'normal' person cannot assassinate someone without checking for degeneration. A 'bad' person can do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory.<br /> Checking for degeneration isn't the same as losing Humanity.<br /> By the system, a &quot;good&quot; person can kill their way through a crowd and still be a &quot;good&quot; person afterwards as long as they feel bad about it (make their Conscience check). And if they have good reason (self defense?) some ST will even give them a bonus or a pass on the roll.<br /> <br /> But it was actually my point that morality is so gray as to lose all meaning across most/all of the WoD lines. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:53:29-08:00","id":1002992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002990#post1002990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory.<br /> Checking for degeneration isn't the same as losing Humanity.<br /> By the system, a &quot;good&quot; person can kill their way through a crowd and still be a &quot;good&quot; person afterwards as long as they feel bad about it (make their Conscience check). And if they have good reason (self defense?) some ST will even give them a bonus or a pass on the roll.<br /> <br /> But it was actually my point that morality is so gray as to lose all meaning across most/all of the WoD lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I think it is important to see when something IS wrong. Like the Impegrium, abuse of metis and the War of Rage(s). However, it doesn't mean I cannot play someone who thinks those were good things. Most of my characters, having been raised by garou, think of humanity in not so nice terms at the best of times. It does not stop me from thinking it is wrong, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:43:08-08:00","id":1003016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997324-debate-the-impergium?p=1002992#post1002992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I think it is important to see when something IS wrong. Like the Impegrium, abuse of metis and the War of Rage(s). However, it doesn't mean I cannot play someone who thinks those were good things. Most of my characters, having been raised by garou, think of humanity in not so nice terms at the best of times. It does not stop me from thinking it is wrong, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agreed. Though even being a human raised by humans I think humans are pretty messed up. And in setting they're certainly worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:19:13-08:00","id":1003182,"title":"","content":"I would think that it would be hard to really justify anything that occurred before fifty years ago. People use the lame excuse that ;it was another time' or 'we cannot judge people in the past', but it is just because they do not want to be judged by people in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}